WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
[The film was] really really inspiring to watch - one of
the main themes was obviously Meg overcoming

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:08.580
her insecurities, mm-hmm, what was the
biggest insecurity each of you had at

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.389
that age and how did you overcome it? I
did not like the way that I looked, I

00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:17.699
think, that was a big issue I had I grew
up in an area where the

00:00:17.699 --> 00:00:22.130
sort of ideal of beauty was very
different than what I looked like and

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.910
that was something that started at a
young age and then carried on and I

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.140
think later in my 20s as I got sort of
more professional success and was

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.260
surrounded by people who didn't have
this, and moved away from the place I

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.129
grew up, I think I that I and definitely
my 30s I gained more confidence but I

00:00:38.129 --> 00:00:43.710
still struggle with it but I that was my
big fear back then. Mine too - I wore

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:50.129
coke-bottle cat eye glasses, I
hated them so much I went to my mother

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.399
saying, "gee could I please get a pair of
octagon glasses?"

00:00:53.399 --> 00:01:06.689
She said we couldn't afford it so I
accidentally staged a robbery... *Laughter* And broke them...I had myself put in the hospital...

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:10.920
I thought was the reason why I was not
being accepted and ended up having to

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.210
get some new glasses so yeah. Well your glasses look amazing today! Thank you, and now I

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:21.150
wear them all the time but yeah I hated
glasses. I had glasses too, I hated my glasses I was so

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:26.100
embarrassed. I was embarrassed of my glasses.
I was a late developer so when I was

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:31.680
14 all the other girls had boobs and
stuff and I was so embarrassed that I

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.890
didn't. I would hide in the locker room
and change my clothes in a way that no

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:39.810
one would ever see my body. Wow. I had a similar thing with the glasses.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:45.420
Really? Yeah...What's one quote that you
live by,  each of you?

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:52.950
Erm, my mother said uh "you cannot say I
love you before you can say I" which I

00:01:52.950 --> 00:02:02.399
think is, very useful. My mother used to always say "if you
want something done do it yourself". True. Uh, the

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:06.930
woman who was like a mother to me Maya
Angelou has a wonderful poem called "To

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.930
Our Grandmothers' and in the poem she
says "When you learn,

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:23.500
teach, when you get, give." That's beautiful. 
I'm getting emotional! When you learn, teach, I love that. When you learn, teach, when you get, give.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.000
Obviously I can imagine you

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.409
guys had lots of fun on set together...
What's your favourite memory from working

00:02:28.409 --> 00:02:35.420
together on this, would you say? The first
thing that came to mind was Mindy falling... *Laughter*

00:02:37.969 --> 00:02:42.239
That's so mean! This is this is just a funny memory I
don't know if it's anybody's favourite memory

00:02:42.239 --> 00:02:46.169
but I'll say it was my favourite too. We
were in, we've been to so many amazing

00:02:46.169 --> 00:02:49.379
places in this movie, I mean Ava really gave us the gift of seeing the

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:55.169
world and for me seeing the different
worlds of green screen and being in

00:02:55.169 --> 00:02:58.139
a fantasy movie for the first time,
but there was a scene we were just doing a

00:02:58.139 --> 00:03:03.299
very ordinary shot in the backyard of a
house and we're sitting and the three of

00:03:03.299 --> 00:03:08.700
us were saying goodbye to Meg and we shot
this after we had shot all of our stuff

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.049
in the States and we're standing there
and Oprah's telling her, giving her

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:15.419
advice about you know we're saying
goodbye and we're parting words and my

00:03:15.419 --> 00:03:20.069
costume, it was one of my bigger costumes
and for some reason it just I think I

00:03:20.069 --> 00:03:23.849
lost my footing because we wore these
really high stiletto shoes and I slowly

00:03:23.849 --> 00:03:30.389
fell, out of frame behind them as Oprah
is talking and Oprah can kind of see me but doesn't, you just didn't want to...

00:03:30.389 --> 00:03:47.159
It's just her and this
great big quilted skirt, just falling...Like a wedding cake. And Mindy kept going, "I'm falling, I'm falling..."

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:51.780
One of my favourite memories is being in the
trailer one morning and I brought all of

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:56.220
these English muffins that I wanted everybody to sample. And we're just toasting so many

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:59.639
muffins that the fire alarm goes off and
everybody comes running to the

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:06.810
trailers because we're gonna set the
trailer on fire... Toasting muffins. But these

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:13.319
muffins, oh my Gosh. I could have one right now. She had this jelly... Oh the jelly! We ate a lot. We enjoyed ourselves.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:18.079
Oh my God, I wish I was there with you guys.

